## OpenShip — ship log

This project uses OpenShip (the `openship` CLI) to keep a living changelog.

When the user asks to "ship log", "document today", or "close the day":

1. Get the project name: `openship project`
2. Gather the raw material: `openship gather <project>`
3. Summarize into **Added / Modified / Removed** following `openship curate`
   (the "what", not files; short bullets; real numbers or none; omit empty lists).
4. Write the section (body on stdin):
   `printf '%s\n' "$BODY" | openship upsert <project> <YYYY-MM-DD>`
5. Refresh the prose summary:
   `openship read <project> all`  then
   `printf '%s' "$SUMMARY" | openship summary <project>`

To capture a spontaneous idea: `openship idea "..."`.
To read recent work: `openship read <project|all> <days|all>`.
